commit 5adf3426ee53deaf0a45aa9b3116e3188571532d
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 24 09:56:57 2026 +1100

    Import eventlet only for the WSGI server
    
    Only the deprecated Server uses eventlet and greenlet, yet neutron
    imports oslo_service.wsgi everywhere for Loader, Request and
    register_opts. Import them in Server's methods; protocol now defaults
    to None, which still means eventlet.wsgi.HttpProtocol.
    
    The saving also needs eventlet gone from futurist, oslo.utils'
    eventletutils, oslo.messaging's _utils and oslo.privsep (1011795). With
    all of them, neutron's L3 and metadata agents drop eventlet, from 117MB
    to 106MB and 103MB anonymous; its servers keep it through python-ovs.
    
    Prompt: Mikal asked for the rest of the eventlet import chain to be
    fixed, so that neutron's threaded agents stop loading eventlet; this is
    the oslo.service part of it.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (high effort)
    
    Depends-On: https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/devstack/+/1011992
    Change-Id: Id8f23667d2b188af9a51de07ca48eaa5409f0f6f
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

